Package: trigemit-kafka
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, mariadb-server
Description: MariaDB UDF for publishing to Kafka
 TrigEmit-Kafka is a MariaDB user defined function module, loaded by the server
 as a plugin, that lets SQL publish messages to a Kafka cluster.
 .
 The intended use is a trigger calling kafka_send() with a JSON_OBJECT()
 payload, turning row changes into a stream of Kafka events. Publishing is
 asynchronous, so a trigger does not wait for the broker.
 .
 The connection is configured entirely from SQL: kafka_connection_param() sets
 any librdkafka property, which makes SASL and TLS authenticated brokers,
 delivery guarantees and buffering all reachable without rebuilding.
